#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/id #uuid "7caffa88-776d-52e1-8b81-2ebf98aedebc" :question/math-academy-id "e-6122" :question/problem "Let $R = [-1,4]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y) \\, \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that $m_{ij} = M_{ij} = 3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since $m_{ij}=M_{ij}=3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =3(4-(-1))(2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=15 & \\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 15=U(f,P),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/id #uuid "3464909c-5b04-5cb1-96c9-a409fa105bb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9494" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},\\, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute $\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j = (x_m^2 - x_0^2)(y_n-y_0)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that $\\bar{x}_i = \\dfrac 1 2 (x_{i-1}+x_i)$ will always lie between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i,$ and similarly $\\bar{y}_j = \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1}+y_j)$ will always lie between $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + {\\color{blue}2}\\cdot \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1} + y_j) \\leq x_{i} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j},\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + 2y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\leq x_{i} + 2y_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j$ and applying the double summation gives\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\right]\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j + \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(y_{j-1} + y_j\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(3-1)=4 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})(2-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 4+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 20\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/id #uuid "e75f2d8e-c165-5a24-942b-7326d7f11f0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9497" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 12-x-y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle I = \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm dA\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\:\\leq I \\:\\leq U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums. Write down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions $R_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = f(x_{i-1}, y_{j-1}) = 12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d717d9c-0eb4-5131-86ae-5e4b8f971afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + 2y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125949} {:answer/id #uuid "e363426c-a323-5221-9bb4-0ec402d943e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125950} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a7b0c5-5385-547c-8536-1670f2c8b718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + 2y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125951} {:answer/id #uuid "554de992-079d-5725-9c03-00791f0d82eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125952} {:answer/id #uuid "5de4d171-f6cc-5b73-b912-9fbb6401a86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a7b0c5-5385-547c-8536-1670f2c8b718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + 2y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125951} :answer-field/id #uuid "e062ed5e-65af-537d-aae7-bfc420fc0e55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "157470f8-e24e-5ffe-9569-91b340dbb848" :question/math-academy-id "q-123489" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+2y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34daec8f-11eb-5899-af23-7c8346363889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385990} {:answer/id #uuid "c9791c8b-7381-57ac-acff-8778cd3eb8fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385991} {:answer/id #uuid "a47031fa-61d9-5f7b-813b-ada6deb0590e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385992} {:answer/id #uuid "921dd73b-252a-55f7-82de-1ba662abbcd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385993} {:answer/id #uuid "4c697b73-d863-5d47-bf08-c090da5e8c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "921dd73b-252a-55f7-82de-1ba662abbcd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385993} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e65237b-99cb-59cb-8f53-f1cf6730519b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f53517af-8f12-572f-ac12-4e04c2e76dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123737" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4023e224-9660-51a0-9e21-5b7afe7882de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}-8{y}_{j}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385997} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5915cd-1dce-5e7b-a642-71517145c357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}-8{y}_{j-1}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385998} {:answer/id #uuid "7f645aeb-a4dd-5789-a7a1-7965e0e92a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385999} {:answer/id #uuid "076e3d49-d886-539d-b1af-683ac74ab655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386000} {:answer/id #uuid "a13065b7-956f-53c1-adc4-a5ea1a5737d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f645aeb-a4dd-5789-a7a1-7965e0e92a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385999} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa8cd33-ec70-5647-810c-a5ae8afd4bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "405f4221-5ff0-5616-8b3d-b5f05becca90" :question/math-academy-id "q-123740" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,2]\\times [-4,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "965f93e9-dd6b-52aa-bd32-9104d08e86f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386004} {:answer/id #uuid "8328a69d-5e9f-5101-af4c-a0d6b82edd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386005} {:answer/id #uuid "d271ffc5-ceda-5f86-a4d9-f8f4d694a83d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386006} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cd5e9c-c4d2-5d6f-ab7b-c78677daa71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386007} {:answer/id #uuid "21c12d5f-13c9-5aae-ab99-2ec41470c626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "965f93e9-dd6b-52aa-bd32-9104d08e86f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386004} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc209ebc-8cb5-525d-986b-aead72fe2b69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20d27d4e-9ece-5633-8e10-bf16ba96deb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-123741" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [-2,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10+y-3x.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Definition of the Double Integral in Terms of Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89b1ec9-59ec-51e6-a923-018cbf486c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386011} {:answer/id #uuid "6217b638-b09c-54e9-b510-9a6dd11f8901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386012} {:answer/id #uuid "70186d7b-ec0e-5ffc-8a9f-ab3270874850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the options is correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386013} {:answer/id #uuid "3397af36-1ab8-52af-bab6-6c2f3cb2a130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386014} {:answer/id #uuid "0aa36fcf-f972-5192-8198-31079ee94b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aa36fcf-f972-5192-8198-31079ee94b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386015} :answer-field/id #uuid "59fee703-3802-5536-a5c7-6840c6246bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48e328da-8874-5d26-a89b-4390598a0751" :question/math-academy-id "q-123742" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $L(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "645e7f31-6479-5974-ba9c-59a1593f462b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386018} {:answer/id #uuid "4e58385a-6d95-5f4e-b793-41bad8d90d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386019} {:answer/id #uuid "a5566391-5887-5931-ac51-1084acb08df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386020} {:answer/id #uuid "18a37a70-dc7f-5128-98c3-a65ec67c1bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386021} {:answer/id #uuid "b4780a7b-0675-5cb5-8868-06d94aae8b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5566391-5887-5931-ac51-1084acb08df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386020} :answer-field/id #uuid "949a5957-0ee7-5504-a207-1f21d67c7892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4539918d-15a9-5633-94ba-162c54a0312b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123839" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [2,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-3(3-(-1))(5-2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-36\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -36=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-36.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d3dcf6-5518-5670-bc83-0f8c216baa26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386025} {:answer/id #uuid "9512f7c7-6c21-5dbd-bbab-8f44e458e852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386026} {:answer/id #uuid "3883bf7d-2d69-5a5a-802a-eaa5c3bc0052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386027} {:answer/id #uuid "8051af47-5f4a-53a6-9c50-e3c3aad202e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386028} {:answer/id #uuid "bc95eebd-c863-5c9f-a62b-f769557bf4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75d3dcf6-5518-5670-bc83-0f8c216baa26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386025} :answer-field/id #uuid "670398aa-bb0c-52e9-b66b-60a629755f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "212d6373-efba-5135-90cc-77b5fcb91a3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123843" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-2]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =(-2-(-5))(7-3) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=12\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 12=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c401d46-b992-59e6-8863-38ecab593c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386032} {:answer/id #uuid "d19a0965-6c2b-52aa-9a84-abbbe8217290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386033} {:answer/id #uuid "27ede692-5090-5a91-b029-26c5b6640e95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386034} {:answer/id #uuid "4954b87e-acd6-5f5e-b91e-3d89f44e1210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386035} {:answer/id #uuid "658ce99c-4f6c-5011-9089-a627ce1ed6bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4954b87e-acd6-5f5e-b91e-3d89f44e1210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386035} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c955686-849b-5d9f-8887-4249163d5c70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0c22e73-7654-5d07-a6ef-2c5b4606e203" :question/math-academy-id "q-123846" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [4,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =6({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =6(7-1)(6-4) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=72\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 72=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=72.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6deac03f-2f77-5460-9cf8-9a2eda2ae86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "234" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386039} {:answer/id #uuid "2d29142b-1a94-5425-b7a7-5778de06d784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386040} {:answer/id #uuid "3c79e2da-64d0-57b4-9407-5e76830405e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386041} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2edc8a-35ae-58be-84b6-96386a37db72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "306" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386042} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8a6466-736f-5eab-844e-aafc9912be06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e8a6466-736f-5eab-844e-aafc9912be06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386043} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81bd184-da06-5b5c-8a0c-29198780befe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f334c18b-c7f6-5afa-84d2-c8f6b1961318" :question/math-academy-id "q-123872" :question/problem "Let $R=[-4,0]\\times [-5,-2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j}\\le -2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j}\\le -({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{5}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[-({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{5}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le -{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({0}^{2}-(-4)^{2})(-2-(-5))=-48 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-2)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(0-(-4))=-210\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -(-48)-(-210)\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 258\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=258.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc8824b8-8360-5cff-95c5-3b1cfbe5c42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386046} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2f4f5f-ed52-5c84-b5b3-3410387936c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386047} {:answer/id #uuid "12607cb3-376b-5b1f-a3f8-2d29b3a792c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386048} {:answer/id #uuid "e67ec58f-1203-597c-a93b-4de390e6ce5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386049} {:answer/id #uuid "2d53385b-3569-5e5f-93a2-e3b933dab12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d53385b-3569-5e5f-93a2-e3b933dab12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386050} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65d2859-f2b1-5a54-9bde-1036012fc28a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6290d12e-5625-5378-a1c5-40b0a700fc6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123873" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0}) \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j} & \\le -3-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j}) \\\\  & \\le -3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j}\\le -3-2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[-3-2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le -3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2})(2-(-2))=24 \\\\ 3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3({2}^{2}-(-2)^{2})(2-(-1))=0 \\\\ 3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3(2-(-1))(2-(-2))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -36-24-0\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -60\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-60.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83bc6494-39a4-57ae-bad9-645b0de147df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128535} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0a3343-a2a3-5d10-89f0-c9a4b7913fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128536} {:answer/id #uuid "231fbeea-c7bd-52f1-a3f3-0d69514d8fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128537} {:answer/id #uuid "54bf34d6-0d85-594b-8d04-0cf4b5a5fe37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128538} {:answer/id #uuid "587b0d87-0f2a-5589-baa7-43334248e718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54bf34d6-0d85-594b-8d04-0cf4b5a5fe37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128538} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfe3b51-b817-5aad-bf0b-61e7a4be688d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08870289-b60b-524f-b96e-8c75f1f41bc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-72627" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n4\\cdot {x}_{i-1}+2\\cdot {y}_{j-1}\\le 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4\\cdot {x}_{i}+2\\cdot {y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le 2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})(2-0)=64 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(4-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 64+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 80\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2ddd0a8-0864-5d45-85b7-9628f09deb67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386053} {:answer/id #uuid "979edcc5-f7e9-5d25-a26c-e4f8cc8374a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386054} {:answer/id #uuid "6688d98f-2459-57a7-8b15-e42b4aa215ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386055} {:answer/id #uuid "82f8c6de-30d9-5961-8ef4-dfb0094d090d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386056} {:answer/id #uuid "3311fecc-a677-57c3-8e01-bcbc3748c7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2ddd0a8-0864-5d45-85b7-9628f09deb67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386053} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef73560-a1f3-5274-83c1-02d51b804850" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d67b2272-6cb0-5162-9166-f9c0809e3db8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72684" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4$ for all partition $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =4(4-0)(6-2) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=64\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 64=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=64.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d98d56-0dd0-58bb-9328-5f429dbc14ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd567ed-4f92-540a-afd5-9b49525cc17d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386061} {:answer/id #uuid "df386287-2cae-5762-84da-48ae92ab1f6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386062} {:answer/id #uuid "74daab8d-a932-565d-8959-172dac3c88d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386063} {:answer/id #uuid "af81be29-9118-5088-9414-b66bf3328319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74daab8d-a932-565d-8959-172dac3c88d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386063} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbed1845-521e-523a-9287-a8b1d745c45d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b42d7f7-8e5b-51c7-9711-14914c01cbe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72905" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0}) \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1\\le 3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1\\le 3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1\\le \\frac{3}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1\\le 3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le \\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{3}{2}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2})(4-2)=45 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})(4-1)=18 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =(4-1)(4-2)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 45+18-6\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 57\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=57.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using the Mean Value of X and Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c914005-a184-5da1-b324-7bd70d67b11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386067} {:answer/id #uuid "0c0a18fb-690b-5f67-8274-623c26ea90ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-324" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386068} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc1b137-6504-51a8-9e34-5d6b3f69b157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386069} {:answer/id #uuid "faba89cb-0d0c-5e3d-8492-d28a6a54aa71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386070} {:answer/id #uuid "ada1ffaf-d18d-5212-9f86-5555bc1f69db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ada1ffaf-d18d-5212-9f86-5555bc1f69db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386071} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f07878-22a4-50c3-9e66-1bf28f6b3816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44ba02d1-09f0-557c-bc39-57987e983b2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72906" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-1]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le \\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-1)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(3-0)=-180 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})(-1-(-5))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -180+36\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -144\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-144.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f647946-7308-5125-8c30-40bb8c84b6c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386074} {:answer/id #uuid "325bae4a-401d-5ab3-a5d4-7869967ea6d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386075} {:answer/id #uuid "a9034a66-a89e-5bc8-bbcc-74874576e989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386076} {:answer/id #uuid "0f51c298-6c79-523a-89f5-b85b1928b05e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386077} {:answer/id #uuid "03c20b7f-7a89-5360-ab37-3c1852f54906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9034a66-a89e-5bc8-bbcc-74874576e989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386076} :answer-field/id #uuid "25683915-c818-5236-a6fb-4f6aa94c04ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d396205-f6a2-5f67-98a9-fdf447376337" :question/math-academy-id "q-72909" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [1,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-2$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-2(4-1)(4-1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-18\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -18=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-18.\n$$"}]}
